Corollary 2.4: (Singular value decomposition) Let $A$ be a square matrix.
Then there exist unitary matrices $U$ and $V$, and a diagonal matrix $D$ with non-negative entries such that

$$
\begin{equation*}
A=U D V \tag{2.80}
\end{equation*}
$$

The diagonal elements of $D$ are called the singular values of $A$.

